WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.580
With age comes wisdom… and Ugg boots.&nbsp;
For "The Big Bang Theory's" Kaley Cuoco,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.080
Penny’s cleavage-baring tank tops and&nbsp;
Juicy Couture zip-ups didn’t always fit.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.880
"The Big Bang Theory" was on the air for&nbsp;
a total of 12 seasons and 279 episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.680
so it makes sense that the sitcom ended up&nbsp;
changing over so many years. According to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.700
Cinema Blend, the pilot featured completely&nbsp;
different characters, like the much darker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.880
tough-as-nails character Katie,&nbsp;
instead of the gentler Penny.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.620
Early episodes of the show also emphasized&nbsp;
the massive gap between the nerdy scientists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.600
like Leonard and Sheldon, and their hot neighbor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.040
Penny. This slowly changed throughout the show&nbsp;
as the writers took more time to develop the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.200
ensemble cast and flesh out the relationships.&nbsp;
Co-creator Chuck Lorre noted in USA Today,

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.140
"The characters grew. It&nbsp;
expanded the relationships&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.880
and what the characters were capable of doing."

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.120
One thing that especially&nbsp;
changed was how Penny was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.580
treated in the series — and even how she dressed.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.260
In earlier seasons of the show, Penny dressed&nbsp;
sexy, wearing revealing outfits that flashed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.220
cleavage and almost always featured a tank&nbsp;
top. As the seasons ticked by, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.360
the waitress began dressing more formally and&nbsp;
was covered up much more than she used to be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.900
Penny actor Kaley Cuoco has thoughts&nbsp;
on her character's wardrobe evolution,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.480
and her feelings on the shift&nbsp;
are what you might expect.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.020
In an interview with W Magazine,&nbsp;
Cuoco said that at first she didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.334
mind wearing Penny's revealing clothing&nbsp;
during the early seasons of the show.

00:01:19.382 --> 00:01:23.220
"I started Big Bang at 21 years old.&nbsp;
I was the cute girl next door to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.000
nerds [who] was all about booty&nbsp;
shorts and Juicy Couture zip-ups."

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.334
But as Cuoco and Penny got older, the style&nbsp;
didn't feel right for the character anymore.

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:32.421
"All of a sudden, it's like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.421 --> 00:01:36.360
'Can I have a long-sleeve shirt? How&nbsp;
about a slack? How about a loafer?'"

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.580
The Emmy-nominated actor joked about wearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.240
Uggs with shorts all the time and said she&nbsp;
was sick of wearing high heels. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.355
Cuoco doesn't feel like the sexy&nbsp;
clothes took away from her performance.

00:01:46.355 --> 00:01:48.780
"I don't think it was hard to&nbsp;
wear that stuff and be funny.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.180
I think I love being funny no matter what."

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.780
To her, a lot of Penny's comedy&nbsp;
was self-deprecating, which worked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.200
perfectly. Clearly, she can knock out&nbsp;
a comedic performance no matter what,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.680
as we saw in "The Flight Attendant"&nbsp;
and the "Harley Quinn" animated series.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:07.020
While Kaley Cuoco eventually became sick of&nbsp;
wearing heels and miniskirts, co-star Kunal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.820
Nayyar hated Raj's unflattering clothes. Raj&nbsp;
often dresses in a combination of sweater vests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:16.320
windbreakers, and cargo pants that make sense&nbsp;
for a young male geek. Nayyar told Page Six,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.700
"I think the discussion that happened with the&nbsp;
costume designer is that because he's in a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.900
country and because he's a genius at such&nbsp;
a young age, the layers act as protection."

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:29.220
However, if Nayyar's Instagram page is&nbsp;
anything to go by, he tends to dress in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:34.380
elegant and stylish fashion. It's why he told&nbsp;
Deadline in 2019 that he would be burning his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.060
character's cargo pants once the show ended. He&nbsp;
also took on some new television roles where he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:43.380
couldn't be typecast as Raj, including the&nbsp;
Netflix series "Criminal" and the Apple TV+&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:48.180
series "Suspicion." Ultimately, both Cuoco&nbsp;
and Nayyar seem to have transcended their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:53.051
former sitcom characters' style, whether that&nbsp;
involves Juicy Couture zip-ups or windbreakers.

